      <p class="chapter-num">Part 8 · Check yourself</p>
      <h2>Self-check</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="flow">
      <p>Not graded. Tap an answer to see if you got it, and read why. Try again until you get them all.</p>
      <Quiz id="quiz-avl" questions={quiz} />

      <div class="remember">
        <p class="note-label">Key takeaways</p>
        <ol>
          <li>A BST can become a slow chain if values arrive in sorted order.</li>
          <li>Balance factor = height(left) − height(right). Allowed: −1, 0, +1. Fix at ±2.</li>
          <li>An AVL tree is a BST that keeps every balance factor in −1 to +1 using rotations.</li>
          <li>Name the case from the unbalanced node: LL and RR need 1 rotation; LR and RL need 2.</li>
          <li>During a rotation, one child changes parent. Don't lose it.</li>
          <li>Rotations never break the BST rule, so in-order is always sorted.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <p><b>Next lesson:</b> <a href={base + '/itc120/red-black-trees/'}>Red-black trees</a>, another way to keep a BST balanced.</p>

